
//
// Detection: PowerShell Execution Policy Bypass
// Platform: Microsoft Sentinel
// Data source: DeviceProcessEvents
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001
//

DeviceProcessEvents
| where Timestamp >= ago(24h)
| where FileName in~ ("powershell.exe", "pwsh.exe")
| extend CommandLine = tostring(ProcessCommandLine)
| where CommandLine matches regex
    @"(?i)-(?:executionpolicy|ep)\s+['""]?bypass(?:['""]|\s|$)"
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceName,
    AccountName,
    FileName,
    ProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    ProcessId
| order by Timestamp desc


Understand the regex
(?i)-(?:executionpolicy|ep)\s+['""]?bypass(?:['""]|\s|$)


| Pattern | Meaning |
|---|---|
| (?i) | Case-insensitive matching |
| - | Parameter starts with hyphen |
| (?:executionpolicy|ep) | Full or abbreviated parameter |
| \s+ | One or more spaces |
| ['""]? | Optional quote |
| bypass | Matches bypass value |
| (?:['""]|\s|$) | Checks the value boundary |
